;; scenario.aura — deterministic event tape for the mini-orderbook engine.
;;
;; `(scenario-events)` returns a flat list of event STRINGS (one per line,
;; same shape the tape parser in `tape.aura` expects). The engine then
;; parses them via `parse-line` / `build-tape` before matching.
;;
;; The tape is engineered so that running it through the engine produces
;; the canonical output referenced in GOAL.md §2. Specifically we want:
;;   * at least one marketable BUY that crosses the spread → produces trades
;;   * at least one marketable SELL that crosses the spread → produces trades
;;   * a partial fill on one side so a resting order remains
;;   * a CANCEL that actually removes something
;;   * a few resting orders on each side so top-of-book is non-trivial
;;
;; Determinism: fixed ids ("B1".."B3", "S1".."S3", "C1"), fixed prices and
;; quantities, fixed line order. There is no randomness anywhere.
;;
;; Format per line (matches the parser contract in tape.aura):
;;   "NEW BUY  <price> <qty> <id>"
;;   "NEW SELL <price> <qty> <id>"
;;   "CANCEL <id>"

(define (scenario-events)
  (list
   ;; --- seed resting liquidity on both sides -------------------
   "NEW BUY  49 5 B1"
   "NEW BUY  50 3 B2"
   "NEW BUY  48 2 B3"
   "NEW SELL 51 4 S1"
   "NEW SELL 52 2 S2"
   "NEW SELL 53 3 S3"

   ;; --- marketable BUY: lifts 51 (qty 4) then 52 (qty 1 of 2),
   ;;     leaving 1 unit of S2 resting at 52. -------------------
   "NEW BUY  52 5 BUY_X"

   ;; --- marketable SELL: hits 50 (qty 3) fully, then 49
   ;;     (qty 1 of 5), leaving 4 units of B1 resting at 49. ----
   "NEW SELL 49 4 SELL_X"

   ;; --- a smaller marketable BUY that just nicks one unit
   ;;     off the new best ask (S2 resting at 52). -------------
   "NEW BUY  53 1 BUY_Y"

   ;; --- a NON-marketable BUY that rests inside the spread. ----
   "NEW BUY  50 6 B4"

   ;; --- a CANCEL that actually removes a resting order. -------
   "CANCEL B3"))
